From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:46:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: clear carried needs_you with kanban evidence; no
 invariant reports for non-live rows [daveey]

Review 5987589833 on #3735:
- withKanbanEvidence (retained-row refresh and the per-gateway carry) copied and cleared only kanban_* keys, so a
  stale `needs_you` survived a fresh snapshot that omitted it (empty) and kept the row red after its card
  unblocked/archived. needs_you is now part of the kanban evidence set; sameCronSignature compares it too.
- stripeInvariantViolation fired for archived/offline rows whose stripe is null because they are not live; the
  invariant governs live rows only (recordStripeTransition takes `live`).
- card_is_open_human_ask reuses the status-independent leaf _stored_needs_human that _board_rows uses; the
  narrowed needs_you shape (card entries, empty question) is documented.
